speechtext:
But conditions were bad even before then. I know the Prime Minister does not want to bother with anyone, but he knows that the conditions as we depicted them in the debate on the address were not a
22110-235}
bit overdrawn. They have been aggravated by a lack of moisture, I admit. But the conditions were absolutely as we depicted them at that time.

Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-318. Common and colourless window glass: British preferential tariff, 74 per cent; intermediate tariff, 124 per cent; general tariff, 124 per cent. Provided, that the governor in council may, when satisfied that common colourless window glass is being manufactured in Canada in quality and quantity sufficient for Canadian requirements, by order in council direct that there be substituted for this tariff item the following: Common and colourless window- glass:
(a)	in sheets not exceeding 80 square inches in area, per pound: British preferential tariff, If cents; intermediate tariff, If cents; general tariff, If cents;
(b)	in sheets exceeding 80 square inches but not exceeding 120 square inches in area, per pound: British preferential tariff, 2f cents; intermediate tariff, 3 cents; general tariff, 3 cents;
(c)	in sheets exceeding 120 squire inches in area, per pound: British preferential tariff, 3f cents; intermediate tariff, 44 cents; general tariff, 44 cents.
